From ad26c2529c9b812aef90f33e658729d0144bfd0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rigaz29 <ryanbagas27@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 17:46:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fs: add susfs open_redirect, symbol hiding and avc log
 spoofing, stage 4

Port the remaining optional susfs features from the 4.4 non-GKI patch:
- open_redirect: redirect opens and readlinks of marked files to a
  clean copy for app processes, and spoof their /proc/<pid>/maps entry.
- Hide ksu_/susfs_ symbols from /proc/kallsyms.
- Spoof ksu domain SIDs in selinux avc audit logs.

3.10 adaptations:
- 3.10's path_openat() opens the file inside do_last() during the walk
  (5.10 splits it into open_last_lookups()+do_open()), so the redirect
  re-walk first releases the first open via fput()+get_empty_filp();
  otherwise finish_open() would hit BUG_ON(*opened & FILE_OPENED).
- No set_nameidata()/restore_nameidata(); the re-walk calls
  path_init(dfd, fake->name, flags) directly and drops the previous
  base file ref first.
- do_tmpfile() takes dfd/pathname arguments here; the redirect redoes
  path_lookupat() on the fake name after path_put() of the original.
- filename_lookup() in 3.10 fills a struct nameidata, not a path; not
  used by the hooks.
- generic_readlink() is follow_link()+vfs_readlink() based in 3.10;
  the spoof result is kept separate so a non-matching entry falls back
  to the real link instead of returning -ENOENT.
- 3.10 has no show_vma_header_prefix(); the maps spoof prints the
  header inline like show_map_vma() itself does.
- 3.10 has no getname_kernel(); susfs_getname_kernel() builds an
  embedded struct filename the same way getname_flags() does so that
  putname() releases it correctly.
- The avc hook lives in avc_dump_query() (3.10 still formats the query
  there); susfs_ksu_sid/susfs_priv_app_sid are cached in susfs_init()
  via security_secctx_to_secid().
